     "result_text_tail": "om the analysis.\n\nNo corrections were needed. The pack shows the 2027 stress royalty as $0.97M and the analysis as $0.98M; both are roundings of 3,250 \u00d7 $300 = $0.975M, so the deck keeps 0.98. No placeholders remain.\n\n**Remaining QA warnings:**\n- Most pages are denser than the guide suggests. I kept every item from the source rather than drop any, and all text renders at 11 pt or larger.\n- On pp. 4, 8 and 12 the sidebar figures interpret the exhibit rather than being calculated from it.\n- On p. 13 the \"$2.6M\" in the title and on p. 20 the \"65%\" appear only as text. The renderer can't show two-decimal $M values as data points, so tables with those values use exact text, and those numbers are traced on the Calculations sheet.\n\n**Not done:**\n- **No visual check:** I couldn't look at the slides as images. LibreOffice isn't installed and the sandbox blocks driving Keynote, so layout was checked only by the renderer's font measurements. Please open the file and look through it.\n- **Workbook post-step:** I added a step that lists the numbers written in table cells and bullets on each page's workbook sheet, since the renderer only lists numbers it draws as charts or callouts.\n- **No re-check against web pages:** with no web sources, the step that re-opens cited pages wasn't needed.\n\nThe spec and build scripts are in `./build/`; `sh build/make.sh` rebuilds both files.\n\nNext, I can switch the theme (`mono` prints well for a board pack) or replace the Gate 2 volume with a value you set."
    }
